  ('6af8814c-cd88-5de9-ae01-c9b49f004eb1', 'Parashorea warburgii', 'Parashorea', 'warburgii', 'Dipterocarpaceae', 'native', 'Parashorea warburgii is a Philippine native tree in Dipterocarpaceae. CDFP habitat record: Primary lowland forests.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and usually leathery, with pinnate side veins; stipules and venation help separate dipterocarp genera.', 'The trunk is typically straight and resin-bearing; mature bark may become fissured or scaly, but color and texture must be checked for this species.', 'Small bisexual, five-parted flowers are borne in branched clusters; petals, stamens, and calyx lobes require close inspection.', 'The fruit is a one-seeded nut enclosed by a persistent calyx; enlarged wing-like calyx lobes aid wind dispersal and identification.', 'A single recalcitrant seed is enclosed in the nut and normally loses viability quickly if allowed to dry.', 'large', 18, 45, 7, 18, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Critically Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Borneo, Philippines. LUZON: Quezon, MINDANAO: Agusan del Norte, Davao, Davao del Sur.', 'Primary lowland forests.'),
  ('102f3ebe-780b-5429-91ac-9dbe1b85ae35', 'Shorea arsorianoi', 'Shorea', 'arsorianoi', 'Dipterocarpaceae', 'endemic', 'Shorea arsorianoi is a Philippine endemic tree in Dipterocarpaceae. CDFP habitat record: The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and usually leathery, with pinnate side veins; stipules and venation help separate dipterocarp genera.', 'The trunk is typically straight and resin-bearing; mature bark may become fissured or scaly, but color and texture must be checked for this species.', 'Small bisexual, five-parted flowers are borne in branched clusters; petals, stamens, and calyx lobes require close inspection.', 'The fruit is a one-seeded nut enclosed by a persistent calyx; enlarged wing-like calyx lobes aid wind dispersal and identification.', 'A single recalcitrant seed is enclosed in the nut and normally loses viability quickly if allowed to dry.', 'large', 18, 45, 7, 18, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. MINDANAO: Davao, Davao del Norte, Surigao del Sur, SAMAR.', 'The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution.'),
  ('96266b82-cbbb-520a-a28e-29be80cc664c', 'Shorea kathleeniana', 'Shorea', 'kathleeniana', 'Dipterocarpaceae', 'endemic', 'Shorea kathleeniana is a Philippine endemic tree in Dipterocarpaceae. CDFP habitat record: The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution. The accepted-name record was retained from CDFP; the automated Kew exact-name search did not return a direct match, so future taxonomic review is flagged.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and usually leathery, with pinnate side veins; stipules and venation help separate dipterocarp genera.', 'The trunk is typically straight and resin-bearing; mature bark may become fissured or scaly, but color and texture must be checked for this species.', 'Small bisexual, five-parted flowers are borne in branched clusters; petals, stamens, and calyx lobes require close inspection.', 'The fruit is a one-seeded nut enclosed by a persistent calyx; enlarged wing-like calyx lobes aid wind dispersal and identification.', 'A single recalcitrant seed is enclosed in the nut and normally loses viability quickly if allowed to dry.', 'large', 18, 45, 7, 18, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LUZON: Bulacan, Laguna, Quezon, MINDANAO: Surigao del Sur, SAMAR.', 'The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution.'),
  ('cc072673-390f-51a4-9b72-77fc745d3e83', 'Vatica mendozae', 'Vatica', 'mendozae', 'Dipterocarpaceae', 'endemic', 'Vatica mendozae is a Philippine endemic tree in Dipterocarpaceae. CDFP habitat record: The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and usually leathery, with pinnate side veins; stipules and venation help separate dipterocarp genera.', 'The trunk is typically straight and resin-bearing; mature bark may become fissured or scaly, but color and texture must be checked for this species.', 'Small bisexual, five-parted flowers are borne in branched clusters; petals, stamens, and calyx lobes require close inspection.', 'The fruit is a one-seeded nut enclosed by a persistent calyx; enlarged wing-like calyx lobes aid wind dispersal and identification.', 'A single recalcitrant seed is enclosed in the nut and normally loses viability quickly if allowed to dry.', 'medium', 10, 30, 5, 12, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Critically Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LUZON: Quezon.', 'The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution.'),
  ('cead6648-fc39-5ec2-b3d5-eba6aa4c8cd3', 'Vatica pachyphylla', 'Vatica', 'pachyphylla', 'Dipterocarpaceae', 'endemic', 'Vatica pachyphylla is a Philippine endemic tree in Dipterocarpaceae. CDFP habitat record: Scattered in aseasonal, primary dipterocarp forests. 0-80m.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and usually leathery, with pinnate side veins; stipules and venation help separate dipterocarp genera.', 'The trunk is typically straight and resin-bearing; mature bark may become fissured or scaly, but color and texture must be checked for this species.', 'Small bisexual, five-parted flowers are borne in branched clusters; petals, stamens, and calyx lobes require close inspection.', 'The fruit is a one-seeded nut enclosed by a persistent calyx; enlarged wing-like calyx lobes aid wind dispersal and identification.', 'A single recalcitrant seed is enclosed in the nut and normally loses viability quickly if allowed to dry.', 'medium', 10, 30, 5, 12, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines; Philippine DAO category: Critically Endangered', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LUZON: Cagayan, Camarines Norte, Camarines Sur, Quezon, POLILLO, SAMAR.', 'Scattered in aseasonal, primary dipterocarp forests. 0-80m.'),
  ('eb8c560a-4927-5c10-8d5d-a7411caae82d', 'Castanopsis philipensis', 'Castanopsis', 'philipensis', 'Fagaceae', 'endemic', 'Castanopsis philipensis is a Philippine endemic tree in Fagaceae. CDFP habitat record: Forests. 400-1800m.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, leathery, and toothed; lower-surface hairs and venation are useful identification characters.', 'Mature bark is gray to brown and becomes rough, fissured, or scaly.', 'Tiny unisexual flowers occur in upright or spreading catkin-like spikes.', 'The fruit is a nut enclosed partly or completely by a spiny or scaly cupule whose structure helps identify the species.', 'A single large seed fills the nut and is generally best sown fresh.', 'large', 12, 35, 6, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Near Threatened', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. BASILAN, LEYTE, LUZON: Albay, Bulacan, Camarines, Nueva Ecija (photos), Rizal, MINDANAO: Agusan del Norte, Bukidnon, Davao del Sur, Lanao del Sur, MINDORO, PALAWAN, SAMAR.', 'Forests. 400-1800m.'),
  ('b4946dd4-9d85-50bc-8b67-9cec6db0f0dc', 'Lithocarpus apoensis', 'Lithocarpus', 'apoensis', 'Fagaceae', 'endemic', 'Lithocarpus apoensis is a Philippine endemic tree in Fagaceae. CDFP habitat record: Forests. Fl. Mar-Dec; fr. Apr-Sep. (?-)1000-1700m.', 'Leaves are alternate, simple, and leathery with pinnate veins; lower-surface texture and margin characters are useful in identification.', 'Mature trunks develop gray to brown, rough or fissured bark.', 'Tiny unisexual flowers occur in upright or spreading catkin-like spikes.', 'The fruit is an acorn-like nut partly enclosed by a woody cupule whose scales or rings are diagnostic.', 'A single large seed fills the nut and is generally best sown fresh.', 'large', 12, 35, 6, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Near Threatened', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines; Philippine DAO category: Vulnerable', 'Endemic to the Philippines. CATANDUANES, LUZON: Aurora, Laguna, Quezon, Rizal, MINDANAO: Bukidnon, Cotabato, Davao, Davao del Sur, PANAY, SAMAR.', 'Forests. Fl. Mar-Dec; fr. Apr-Sep. (?-)1000-1700m.'),
  ('e30e98a9-b4f9-5e6d-819f-151225b01b9e', 'Lithocarpus mindanaensis', 'Lithocarpus', 'mindanaensis', 'Fagaceae', 'endemic', 'Lithocarpus mindanaensis is a Philippine endemic tree in Fagaceae. CDFP habitat record: Common in Mindanao, scattered in Leyte. Forests. Fl. Oct-Mar; fr. May-Sep. 20-600(-1000)m.', 'Leaves are alternate, simple, and leathery with pinnate veins; lower-surface texture and margin characters are useful in identification.', 'Mature trunks develop gray to brown, rough or fissured bark.', 'Tiny unisexual flowers occur in upright or spreading catkin-like spikes.', 'The fruit is an acorn-like nut partly enclosed by a woody cupule whose scales or rings are diagnostic.', 'A single large seed fills the nut and is generally best sown fresh.', 'large', 12, 35, 6, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Near Threatened', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LEYTE, MINDANAO: Agusan del Norte, Bukidnon, Davao, Davao del Sur, Lanao del Norte, Lanao del Sur, Misamis, Surigao, Surigao del Norte, Zamboanga, Zamboanga del Norte, Zamboanga del Sur.', 'Common in Mindanao, scattered in Leyte. Forests. Fl. Oct-Mar; fr. May-Sep. 20-600(-1000)m.'),
  ('b0114dae-9618-589a-8092-8b49a0cbe087', 'Lithocarpus jordanae', 'Lithocarpus', 'jordanae', 'Fagaceae', 'endemic', 'Lithocarpus jordanae is a Philippine endemic tree in Fagaceae. CDFP habitat record: Mossy forests on the higher mountains, rather common. Fl. Jan, Jul; fr. Aug-Apr. 1200-2400m.', 'Leaves are alternate, simple, and leathery with pinnate veins; lower-surface texture and margin characters are useful in identification.', 'Mature trunks develop gray to brown, rough or fissured bark.', 'Tiny unisexual flowers occur in upright or spreading catkin-like spikes.', 'The fruit is an acorn-like nut partly enclosed by a woody cupule whose scales or rings are diagnostic.', 'A single large seed fills the nut and is generally best sown fresh.', 'large', 12, 35, 6, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Vulnerable', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines; Philippine DAO category: Vulnerable', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LUZON: Abra, Benguet, Ifugao, Kalinga, Mountain Province, Nueva Ecija, Nueva Vizcaya, Quirino.', 'Mossy forests on the higher mountains, rather common. Fl. Jan, Jul; fr. Aug-Apr. 1200-2400m.'),
  ('47fa6de3-5689-51ba-bcb7-bb2c668b84d8', 'Lithocarpus woodii', 'Lithocarpus', 'woodii', 'Fagaceae', 'endemic', 'Lithocarpus woodii is a Philippine endemic tree in Fagaceae. CDFP habitat record: Forests. Fl. Aug-Jun; fr. Apr-Nov. (?-)900-2300m.', 'Leaves are alternate, simple, and leathery with pinnate veins; lower-surface texture and margin characters are useful in identification.', 'Mature trunks develop gray to brown, rough or fissured bark.', 'Tiny unisexual flowers occur in upright or spreading catkin-like spikes.', 'The fruit is an acorn-like nut partly enclosed by a woody cupule whose scales or rings are diagnostic.', 'A single large seed fills the nut and is generally best sown fresh.', 'large', 12, 35, 6, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Vulnerable', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LUZON: Benguet, Mountain Province, Quezon, MINDANAO: Bukidnon, Davao, Davao del Sur, SAMAR.', 'Forests. Fl. Aug-Jun; fr. Apr-Nov. (?-)900-2300m.'),
  ('c361f063-acc7-59ad-a5a2-e4b48d32dd7e', 'Cinnamomum anacardium', 'Cinnamomum', 'anacardium', 'Lauraceae', 'endemic', 'Cinnamomum anacardium is a Philippine endemic tree in Lauraceae. CDFP habitat record: The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution.', 'Leaves are aromatic when crushed and usually show three strong veins arising near the base; arrangement and lower-surface characters separate the genera.', 'Inner bark and twigs are aromatic; avoid harvesting bark from wild trees, especially threatened species.', 'Small pale flowers occur in clustered inflorescences and have the typical laurel-family floral structure.', 'The fruit is a one-seeded drupe seated on a persistent cup-like or shallow receptacle.', 'The single seed is enclosed by the fleshy drupe and is best handled fresh.', 'medium', 8, 25, 4, 12, 'moderate', TRUE, TRUE, 'Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. BATAN, CAMIGUIN DE BABUYANES, LUZON: Cagayan, Ilocos Norte.', 'The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution.'),
  ('69699981-b784-5e55-a6fe-7ed099e33597', 'Cinnamomum ebaloi', 'Cinnamomum', 'ebaloi', 'Lauraceae', 'endemic', 'Cinnamomum ebaloi is a Philippine endemic tree in Lauraceae. CDFP habitat record: The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution.', 'Leaves are aromatic when crushed and usually show three strong veins arising near the base; arrangement and lower-surface characters separate the genera.', 'Inner bark and twigs are aromatic; avoid harvesting bark from wild trees, especially threatened species.', 'Small pale flowers occur in clustered inflorescences and have the typical laurel-family floral structure.', 'The fruit is a one-seeded drupe seated on a persistent cup-like or shallow receptacle.', 'The single seed is enclosed by the fleshy drupe and is best handled fresh.', 'medium', 8, 25, 4, 12, 'moderate', TRUE, TRUE, 'Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LUZON: Bataan, MINDANAO: Lanao del Norte.', 'The CDFP checklist record gives no additional habitat sentence beyond its Philippine distribution.'),
  ('d2842402-b3f1-5e03-8830-c78252537a67', 'Cinnamomum lanaoense', 'Cinnamomum', 'lanaoense', 'Lauraceae', 'endemic', 'Cinnamomum lanaoense is a Philippine endemic tree in Lauraceae. CDFP habitat record: L.L.Co: Known only from the type collection.', 'Leaves are aromatic when crushed and usually show three strong veins arising near the base; arrangement and lower-surface characters separate the genera.', 'Inner bark and twigs are aromatic; avoid harvesting bark from wild trees, especially threatened species.', 'Small pale flowers occur in clustered inflorescences and have the typical laurel-family floral structure.', 'The fruit is a one-seeded drupe seated on a persistent cup-like or shallow receptacle.', 'The single seed is enclosed by the fleshy drupe and is best handled fresh.', 'medium', 8, 25, 4, 12, 'moderate', TRUE, TRUE, 'Critically Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. MINDANAO: Lanao.', 'L.L.Co: Known only from the type collection.'),
