  ('c67bda14-0f9d-506b-8e0f-8812b2d3f2b8', 'Cinnamomum rupestre', 'Cinnamomum', 'rupestre', 'Lauraceae', 'endemic', 'Cinnamomum rupestre is a Philippine endemic tree in Lauraceae. CDFP habitat record: 0-1000m.', 'Leaves are aromatic when crushed and usually show three strong veins arising near the base; arrangement and lower-surface characters separate the genera.', 'Inner bark and twigs are aromatic; avoid harvesting bark from wild trees, especially threatened species.', 'Small pale flowers occur in clustered inflorescences and have the typical laurel-family floral structure.', 'The fruit is a one-seeded drupe seated on a persistent cup-like or shallow receptacle.', 'The single seed is enclosed by the fleshy drupe and is best handled fresh.', 'medium', 8, 25, 4, 12, 'moderate', TRUE, TRUE, 'Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines; Philippine DAO category: Endangered', 'Endemic to the Philippines. PALAWAN.', '0-1000m.'),
  ('38cd092a-2fba-5173-ab18-3ac23813d4e2', 'Madhuca multiflora', 'Madhuca', 'multiflora', 'Sapotaceae', 'endemic', 'Madhuca multiflora is a Philippine endemic tree in Sapotaceae. CDFP habitat record: Lowland primary rainforests.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and leathery, often crowded toward twig ends; close parallel side veins may be visible.', 'Cut bark and twigs exude white latex; destructive bark sampling should be avoided, especially for threatened taxa.', 'Small bisexual flowers occur singly or in compact clusters in the leaf axils or on older twigs.', 'The fruit is a fleshy berry, often with a persistent calyx at the base.', 'One or several relatively large, glossy seeds are enclosed in the pulp and should normally be sown fresh.', 'large', 10, 35, 5, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Vulnerable', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. ?HOMONHON, LUZON: Bataan, Nueva Ecija, Quezon, Rizal, MINDANAO: Lanao, Lanao del Sur, PANAY, POLILLO.', 'Lowland primary rainforests.'),
  ('3975a5b9-c831-57e8-bb6b-7e1f701b5c2a', 'Palaquium bataanense', 'Palaquium', 'bataanense', 'Sapotaceae', 'endemic', 'Palaquium bataanense is a Philippine endemic tree in Sapotaceae. CDFP habitat record: Dry hill forests at low elevation. Recorded at 700-850m in Lanao. Fl. Jan, Mar, Oct; fr. Mar, May, Jun.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and leathery, often crowded toward twig ends; close parallel side veins may be visible.', 'Cut bark and twigs exude white latex; destructive bark sampling should be avoided, especially for threatened taxa.', 'Small bisexual flowers occur singly or in compact clusters in the leaf axils or on older twigs.', 'The fruit is a fleshy berry, often with a persistent calyx at the base.', 'One or several relatively large, glossy seeds are enclosed in the pulp and should normally be sown fresh.', 'large', 10, 35, 5, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Vulnerable', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines; Philippine DAO category: Other Threatened Species', 'Endemic to the Philippines. BABUYAN ISLS, BATANES, BORACAY (photos), CAMIGUIN, CAMIGUIN DE BABUYANES, CEBU (photos), LUZON: Bataan, Camarines, MINDANAO: Lanao, PALAWAN, SIBUYAN.', 'Dry hill forests at low elevation. Recorded at 700-850m in Lanao. Fl. Jan, Mar, Oct; fr. Mar, May, Jun.'),
  ('43837a41-1791-55d7-a3af-062981c7466a', 'Palaquium mindanaense', 'Palaquium', 'mindanaense', 'Sapotaceae', 'endemic', 'Palaquium mindanaense is a Philippine endemic tree in Sapotaceae. CDFP habitat record: Lowland primary rainforests.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and leathery, often crowded toward twig ends; close parallel side veins may be visible.', 'Cut bark and twigs exude white latex; destructive bark sampling should be avoided, especially for threatened taxa.', 'Small bisexual flowers occur singly or in compact clusters in the leaf axils or on older twigs.', 'The fruit is a fleshy berry, often with a persistent calyx at the base.', 'One or several relatively large, glossy seeds are enclosed in the pulp and should normally be sown fresh.', 'large', 10, 35, 5, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Critically Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines; Philippine DAO category: Other Threatened Species', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LUZON: Quezon, MINDANAO: Cotabato, Lanao.', 'Lowland primary rainforests.'),
  ('15cb72e6-c0c9-59be-8b94-0aab6e98258d', 'Palaquium philippense', 'Palaquium', 'philippense', 'Sapotaceae', 'endemic', 'Palaquium philippense is a Philippine endemic tree in Sapotaceae. CDFP habitat record: Common in lowland and medium elevation primary forests. Fl. Aug-Sep.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and leathery, often crowded toward twig ends; close parallel side veins may be visible.', 'Cut bark and twigs exude white latex; destructive bark sampling should be avoided, especially for threatened taxa.', 'Small bisexual flowers occur singly or in compact clusters in the leaf axils or on older twigs.', 'The fruit is a fleshy berry, often with a persistent calyx at the base.', 'One or several relatively large, glossy seeds are enclosed in the pulp and should normally be sown fresh.', 'large', 10, 35, 5, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Least Concern', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines; Philippine DAO category: Other Threatened Species', 'Endemic to the Philippines. CATANDUANES, JOLO, LEYTE, LUZON: Albay, Bataan, Batangas, Bulacan, Camarines Sur, Ilocos Norte, Isabela, Laguna, NCR, Pangasinan, Quezon, Rizal, Sorsogon, Tarlac, Zambales (photos), MINDANAO: Bukidnon, Davao, Davao del Sur, Misamis Occidental, Zamboanga, MINDORO, NEGROS, PANAY, SAMAR.', 'Common in lowland and medium elevation primary forests. Fl. Aug-Sep.'),
  ('ef51af46-2126-5f85-b63d-c6be18c7382c', 'Palaquium sorsogonense', 'Palaquium', 'sorsogonense', 'Sapotaceae', 'endemic', 'Palaquium sorsogonense is a Philippine endemic tree in Sapotaceae. CDFP habitat record: Lowland primary forests, swampy habitats, riverine forests, etc. Fl. Dec.', 'Leaves are simple, alternate, and leathery, often crowded toward twig ends; close parallel side veins may be visible.', 'Cut bark and twigs exude white latex; destructive bark sampling should be avoided, especially for threatened taxa.', 'Small bisexual flowers occur singly or in compact clusters in the leaf axils or on older twigs.', 'The fruit is a fleshy berry, often with a persistent calyx at the base.', 'One or several relatively large, glossy seeds are enclosed in the pulp and should normally be sown fresh.', 'large', 10, 35, 5, 16, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Vulnerable', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. BILIRAN, CATANDUANES, HOMONHON, LEYTE, LUZON: Cagayan, Camarines Norte, Camarines Sur, Quezon, Sorsogon, SAMAR.', 'Lowland primary forests, swampy habitats, riverine forests, etc. Fl. Dec.'),
  ('22040b05-0b65-56fc-a835-35775a547df4', 'Canarium euryphyllum', 'Canarium', 'euryphyllum', 'Burseraceae', 'endemic', 'Canarium euryphyllum is a Philippine endemic tree in Burseraceae. CDFP habitat record: 0-800(-1700)m.', 'Leaves are alternate and usually pinnate, with aromatic resin noticeable when twigs or leaf stalks are bruised.', 'The bark contains aromatic resin; its color and fissuring vary with age and should be checked on verified mature material.', 'Small male, female, or bisexual flowers are grouped in branched inflorescences.', 'The fruit is a fleshy drupe that may split or change color at maturity, exposing a hard stone.', 'One or more seeds are protected by the hard inner fruit layer and are commonly dispersed by animals.', 'large', 12, 35, 6, 16, 'moderate', TRUE, TRUE, 'Least Concern', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. BUCAS GRANDE, CATANDUANES, CEBU (photos), DINAGAT, HOMONHON, LEYTE, LUZON: Aurora, Camarines Norte, Camarines Sur, Isabela, Laguna, Quezon, Sorsogon, Zambales, MINDANAO: Bukidnon, Davao del Sur, Surigao, MINDORO, NEGROS, PALAWAN, PANAY, SAMAR, SIBUYAN.', '0-800(-1700)m.'),
  ('4c9434ca-d65a-5f5a-83de-02c148445a67', 'Canarium gracile', 'Canarium', 'gracile', 'Burseraceae', 'endemic', 'Canarium gracile is a Philippine endemic tree in Burseraceae. CDFP habitat record: Throughout the Philippines except Palawan. Forests. 0-400(-600)m.', 'Leaves are alternate and usually pinnate, with aromatic resin noticeable when twigs or leaf stalks are bruised.', 'The bark contains aromatic resin; its color and fissuring vary with age and should be checked on verified mature material.', 'Small male, female, or bisexual flowers are grouped in branched inflorescences.', 'The fruit is a fleshy drupe that may split or change color at maturity, exposing a hard stone.', 'One or more seeds are protected by the hard inner fruit layer and are commonly dispersed by animals.', 'large', 12, 35, 6, 16, 'moderate', TRUE, TRUE, 'Least Concern', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LEYTE, LUZON: Albay, Isabela, Laguna, Quezon, Sorsogon, MINDANAO: Agusan del Norte, Davao Oriental, Davao del Sur, MINDORO, POLILLO, SAMAR.', 'Throughout the Philippines except Palawan. Forests. 0-400(-600)m.'),
  ('eaef4bb2-f52f-53ff-ac87-d4cb67023e8c', 'Canarium luzonicum', 'Canarium', 'luzonicum', 'Burseraceae', 'native', 'Canarium luzonicum is a Philippine native tree in Burseraceae. CDFP habitat record: Common in primary forests at low and medium elevation.', 'Leaves are alternate and usually pinnate, with aromatic resin noticeable when twigs or leaf stalks are bruised.', 'The bark contains aromatic resin; its color and fissuring vary with age and should be checked on verified mature material.', 'Small male, female, or bisexual flowers are grouped in branched inflorescences.', 'The fruit is a fleshy drupe that may split or change color at maturity, exposing a hard stone.', 'One or more seeds are protected by the hard inner fruit layer and are commonly dispersed by animals.', 'large', 12, 35, 6, 16, 'moderate', TRUE, TRUE, 'Near Threatened', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines; Philippine DAO category: Other Threatened Species', 'Pacific Ocean, Philippines. ALABAT, BOHOL, DINAGAT, LUZON: Apayao (photos), Bataan, Cagayan, Camarines Sur, Cavite, Ilocos Sur, Isabela, La Union, Laguna, NCR, Quezon, Rizal, Zambales (photos), MASBATE, MINDANAO: Agusan del Norte, Bukidnon, MINDORO, NEGROS (photos), PALAWAN (photos), SAMAR, TICAO.', 'Common in primary forests at low and medium elevation.'),
  ('88da1ebb-d0a5-5482-a0b6-a4f0a243e538', 'Protium connarifolium', 'Protium', 'connarifolium', 'Burseraceae', 'endemic', 'Protium connarifolium is a Philippine endemic tree in Burseraceae. CDFP habitat record: Forests along streams. 0-600m.', 'Leaves are alternate and usually pinnate, with aromatic resin noticeable when twigs or leaf stalks are bruised.', 'The bark contains aromatic resin; its color and fissuring vary with age and should be checked on verified mature material.', 'Small male, female, or bisexual flowers are grouped in branched inflorescences.', 'The fruit is a fleshy drupe that may split or change color at maturity, exposing a hard stone.', 'One or more seeds are protected by the hard inner fruit layer and are commonly dispersed by animals.', 'large', 12, 35, 6, 16, 'moderate', TRUE, TRUE, 'Vulnerable', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines; Philippine DAO category: Vulnerable', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LUZON: Camarines Sur, PALAWAN.', 'Forests along streams. 0-600m.'),
  ('53a9b925-dc28-5c2f-bbe0-635b0090a7d9', 'Garcinia busuangaensis', 'Garcinia', 'busuangaensis', 'Clusiaceae', 'endemic', 'Garcinia busuangaensis is a Philippine endemic tree in Clusiaceae. CDFP habitat record: Dry forests at low elevation.', 'Leaves are opposite, simple, entire, and leathery, with close parallel side veins.', 'Cut bark and twigs produce yellowish latex, an important Garcinia field character.', 'Small thick-petaled flowers may be male or female and occur singly or in short clusters.', 'The fruit is a fleshy berry with a persistent calyx; mature color and surface texture help distinguish species.', 'Several large seeds are usually surrounded by pulp.', 'medium', 8, 25, 4, 12, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Critically Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. BUSUANGA, LUZON: Sorsogon, PALAWAN (photos).', 'Dry forests at low elevation.'),
  ('87eceb06-b929-530b-9b12-6378c8053722', 'Garcinia luzoniensis', 'Garcinia', 'luzoniensis', 'Clusiaceae', 'endemic', 'Garcinia luzoniensis is a Philippine endemic tree in Clusiaceae. CDFP habitat record: Primary forests at low elevation.', 'Leaves are opposite, simple, entire, and leathery, with close parallel side veins.', 'Cut bark and twigs produce yellowish latex, an important Garcinia field character.', 'Small thick-petaled flowers may be male or female and occur singly or in short clusters.', 'The fruit is a fleshy berry with a persistent calyx; mature color and surface texture help distinguish species.', 'Several large seeds are usually surrounded by pulp.', 'medium', 8, 25, 4, 12, 'slow', TRUE, TRUE, 'Endangered', 'IUCN Red List category reported by Co''s Digital Flora of the Philippines', 'Endemic to the Philippines. LUZON: Laguna, Quezon, SIBUYAN.', 'Primary forests at low elevation.'),
